Whisper: ClickFix protection preferences (clipguard.*)

What: adds the clipguard.mode (block/warn/off), clipguard.user_copy_notice and
clipguard.strict_script_copy static preferences.
Why: these control Whisper's ClickFix protection. They are static prefs so the C++ in
widget/ and toolkit/components/clipguard can read them cheaply on every clipboard write.
The behaviour itself is off unless the clipguard component is built (patches 0041-0043);
clipguard.mode defaults to block.
---
--- a/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
+++ b/modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml
@@ -2438,6 +2438,31 @@
   mirror: always
 
 #---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+# Prefs starting with "clipguard." (Whisper's ClickFix protection)
+#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+
+# What to do when a page puts a command on the clipboard that the person did not
+# select and that is not on screen: 0 block (default), 1 warn but copy, 2 off.
+- name: clipguard.mode
+  type: uint32_t
+  value: 0
+  mirror: always
+
+# Show a one-time notice in the address bar when the person copies a command that
+# looks like one used to install malware (their own Ctrl+C, so never blocked).
+- name: clipguard.user_copy_notice
+  type: bool
+  value: true
+  mirror: always
+
+# Ask about every command a script writes, not only those that are not on screen.
+# Off by default: it would prompt on ordinary documentation copy buttons.
+- name: clipguard.strict_script_copy
+  type: bool
+  value: false
+  mirror: always
+
+#---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 # Prefs starting with "consoleservice."
 #---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
